Refs: #
# <type>(<scope>): <short summary>
#
# Types:
#   feat     = new feature (minor version bump)
#   fix      = bug fix (patch version bump)
#   docs     = documentation only changes
#   perf     = performance improvement
#   refactor = code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   test     = adding or updating tests
#   chore    = maintenance, tooling, formatting, packaging
#
# Scopes (Fontshow):
#   core       = core pipeline, data flow, orchestration
#   cli        = cli interface
#   dev        = development and debug tools, scripts
#   schema     = json schema definition and data validation
#   dump       = dump_fonts tool
#   parser     = parse_font_inventory tool
#   catalog    = create_catalog tool
#   validation = validation tools
#   docs       = documentation (MkDocs, README, architecture)
#   output     = output format
#   config     = configuration files
#   build      = build system / github
#   git        = git configuration
#   dev        = development (tooling, hooks, scripts)
#   ci         = CI / GitHub Actions
#   release    = versioning, tags, changelog
#
# Examples:
#   feat(core): add inventory validation option
#   docs(docs): document schema evolution rules
#   fix(catalog): handle missing family names gracefully
#   chore(core): convert Fontshow into a proper Python package
#
# Breaking changes:
#   Add "!" after the type or include "BREAKING CHANGE:" in the body.
#
#   feat!(core): change inventory schema to v2.0
#
# Body (optional):
#   Explain WHY, not WHAT.
#
# Footer (optional):
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description>
